      "writtenOn": "2017-09-28T13:05:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the current code base, the linkage you are referring to, is actually the ONT logical port number. In order for this linkage to work it is assumed the ONT logical port number is equal to the CVID and that the CVID value is populated in the ONT device.vlan field. As long as these assumptions are true multiple ONTs can be supported on a PON. That being said, these assumptions are not viable going forward and in fact are broken when provisioning via the xPON infrastructure. As a result, the default flow rules that passed to the ONT are broken. I agree that the VLAN configuration should come from ONOS and I opened VOL-460  to track this issue. Since ONOS has the required VLAN configuration I would like to see a solution where ONOS pushes the required VLAN values to vOLTHA. I like the idea of using the venet interface due to it’s one-to-one mapping to UNI but I think we also need to agree on how ONOS will push the required VLAN configuration to voltha/ONOS - possibly via flow rules when a logical port (vent) is created. I believe the current ONOS VLAN provisioning is associated with the logical port.",
